@flexiarg aif/permission-to-revise-the-prediction-after-acting
@title After The Work Is Done, The Prediction May Be Revised; Say So Rather Than Hold To The Earlier Plan
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-R5oe8D turn-rAcshX
@parent aif/grounded-actuation-not-reobservation
@context A plan or prediction was stated before acting; acting changed the world.

! conclusion: After the action, state the old prediction, what changed, and the new direction, and proceed on the new one.

  + IF:
    The operator says it is absolutely okay if the prediction shifts after the work.

  + HOWEVER:
    An agent that holds to its earlier prediction ignores what the action showed; one that shifts silently hides why.

  + THEN:
    After the action, state the old prediction, what changed, and the new direction, and proceed on the new one.

  + BECAUSE:
    Acting changes the world, so the next belief should differ; saying what changed keeps the update checkable.
